        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Induction is one of the safest ways to cook at home. There is no flame, no combustion in the kitchen, and the glass only gets hot from the pan sitting on it. The magnetic field is non-ionizing, contained mostly in the pan and gone within inches, and good habits like centering right-sized pans keep it that way.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The one firm exception is implanted cardiac devices and similar active implants. If that applies to you or someone in your home, talk to your doctor and check the device maker's guidance before you buy. For everyone else, the remaining risks are the same hot pans and hot oil every cooktop has, and fewer of them.
          </p>
